WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.373
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.673 --> 00:00:09.071
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.371 --> 00:00:16.203
Unit fourteen: Traditional Arts. In this unit, you will describe traditional Khmer arts and what they need.

4
00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:18.763
Apsara dance.

5
00:00:19.463 --> 00:00:23.541
Apsara dance means a classical Khmer dance with graceful hand movements.

6
00:00:23.841 --> 00:00:26.468
Apsara dance is famous around the world.

7
00:00:27.168 --> 00:00:30.250
Your turn. Say: Apsara dance.

8
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:34.415
Apsara dance.

9
00:00:35.417 --> 00:00:36.209
Dancer.

10
00:00:36.909 --> 00:00:39.024
Dancer means a person who dances.

11
00:00:39.324 --> 00:00:41.347
The dancer moves her fingers slowly.

12
00:00:42.047 --> 00:00:44.920
Your turn. Say: Dancer.

13
00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:48.435
Dancer.

14
00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:50.335
Costume.

15
00:00:51.035 --> 00:00:53.592
Costume means special clothes for a show.

16
00:00:53.892 --> 00:00:55.740
Her golden costume is beautiful.

17
00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:59.255
Your turn. Say: Costume.

18
00:01:01.955 --> 00:01:02.747
Costume.

19
00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:04.589
Silk.

20
00:01:05.289 --> 00:01:08.205
Silk means soft shiny cloth made by silkworms.

21
00:01:08.505 --> 00:01:10.702
Khmer silk is soft and colorful.

22
00:01:11.402 --> 00:01:13.753
Your turn. Say: Silk.

23
00:01:16.453 --> 00:01:17.222
Silk.

24
00:01:18.217 --> 00:01:19.009
Weaving.

25
00:01:19.709 --> 00:01:22.684
Weaving means making cloth by crossing threads.

26
00:01:22.984 --> 00:01:24.751
My aunt does silk weaving at home.

27
00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.790
Your turn. Say: Weaving.

28
00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.305
Weaving.

29
00:01:32.317 --> 00:01:33.562
Shadow puppets.

30
00:01:34.262 --> 00:01:38.525
Shadow puppets means flat leather figures that make shadows on a screen.

31
00:01:38.825 --> 00:01:40.767
We watched shadow puppets at night.

32
00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:44.421
Your turn. Say: Shadow puppets.

33
00:01:47.121 --> 00:01:48.459
Shadow puppets.

34
00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:50.300
Tradition.

35
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.182
Tradition means something people have done for a very long time.

36
00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:57.401
Weaving is a family tradition.

37
00:01:58.101 --> 00:02:00.916
Your turn. Say: Tradition.

38
00:02:03.616 --> 00:02:04.535
Tradition.

39
00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:06.389
Skill.

40
00:02:07.089 --> 00:02:09.854
Skill means an ability you get by practising.

41
00:02:10.154 --> 00:02:11.910
Dancing needs a lot of skill.

42
00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:15.448
Your turn. Say: Skill.

43
00:02:18.148 --> 00:02:19.010
Skill.

44
00:02:20.017 --> 00:02:22.016
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:22.316 --> 00:02:25.604
Sreypich, what do you need to become an Apsara dancer?

46
00:02:26.917 --> 00:02:28.928
You need to practise every day.

47
00:02:30.217 --> 00:02:31.856
Do you need a special costume?

48
00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.544
Yes, you need a golden costume and a crown.

49
00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:38.374
What about silk weaving?

50
00:02:39.683 --> 00:02:42.089
You need silk thread and a lot of patience!

51
00:02:43.383 --> 00:02:47.577
Grammar focus: Need plus noun and to plus verb.

52
00:02:47.877 --> 00:02:51.191
Dancers need a costume. You need to practise every day.

53
00:02:51.491 --> 00:02:55.232
After 'need', use a noun (a thing) or 'to' + verb (an action).

54
00:02:56.217 --> 00:02:59.055
Now read and listen. Keeping Our Arts Alive.

55
00:02:59.355 --> 00:03:02.039
Cambodia has many beautiful traditional arts.

56
00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:06.406
Apsara dancers need to practise for many years.

57
00:03:07.717 --> 00:03:09.832
They need a golden costume made of silk.

58
00:03:11.117 --> 00:03:14.161
Silk weaving and shadow puppets are old traditions too.

59
00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:19.644
Young people need to learn these skills to keep our culture alive.

60
00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.451
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:23.751 --> 00:03:25.542
Dancers need blank every day.

62
00:03:25.842 --> 00:03:30.134
A, to practise. B, practise. C, practising.

63
00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.405
The answer is A: to practise.

64
00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:40.021
Special clothes for a show are a blank.

65
00:03:40.321 --> 00:03:43.405
A, costume. B, silk. C, skill.

66
00:03:47.417 --> 00:03:49.497
The answer is A: costume.

67
00:03:50.983 --> 00:03:53.621
Making cloth by crossing threads is blank.

68
00:03:53.921 --> 00:03:57.703
A, weaving. B, dancing. C, painting.

69
00:04:01.717 --> 00:04:03.751
The answer is A: weaving.

70
00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:10.250
Now it's your turn to speak. Which traditional art do you like? What do you need to learn it?

71
00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:21.221
I like Apsara dance. To learn it, you need a good teacher, and you need to practise every day.

72
00:04:21.521 --> 00:04:23.509
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:24.517 --> 00:04:30.083
Great work today! You learned eight new words and need plus noun and to plus verb.

74
00:04:30.383 --> 00:04:34.719
Today's value is cultural pride. Be proud of Khmer festivals and traditions.

75
00:04:35.019 --> 00:04:37.509
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:37.809 --> 00:04:40.240
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

